    <widget class="QTabWidget" name="settings_tabs">
     <widget class="QWidget" name="assumptions_tab">
      <attribute name="title">
       <string>Assumptions</string>
      </attribute>
      <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="assumptionsLayout">
       <item>
        <widget class="QScrollArea" name="assumptions_scroll">
         <property name="widgetResizable">
          <bool>true</bool>
         </property>
         <property name="frameShape">
          <enum>QFrame::Shape::NoFrame</enum>
         </property>
         <widget class="QWidget" name="assumptions_content">
          <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="assumptionsContentLayout">
           <property name="leftMargin">
            <number>3</number>
           </property>
           <property name="rightMargin">
            <number>3</number>
           </property>
           <property name="topMargin">
            <number>3</number>
           </property>
           <property name="bottomMargin">
            <number>3</number>
           </property>
           <item><widget class="QLabel" name="assumptions_heading_0"><property name="text"><string>Scope and geometry</string></property><property name="styleSheet"><string>font-weight:600; color:#164f8a;</string></property></widget></item><item><widget class="QLabel" name="assumptions_text_0"><property name="textFormat"><enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum></property><property name="text"><string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;• Cylindrical pressure vessel stress assessment for internal or external pressure, open or capped ends and optional uniform axial load.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;• Any two geometry dimensions may be entered; the third is derived. For independent OD and ID, the original minimum OD / maximum ID basis is retained. For diameter and thickness inputs, physically possible geometries are evaluated and the geometry governing the largest utilisation is selected. All stresses refer to that one geometry, not independent envelopes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string></property><property name="wordWrap"><bool>true</bool></property></widget></item>
<item><spacer name="assumptionsSectionGap1"><property name="orientation"><enum>Qt::Orientation::Vertical</enum></property><property name="sizeType"><enum>QSizePolicy::Fixed</enum></property><property name="sizeHint" stdset="0"><size><width>20</width><height>20</height></size></property></spacer></item><item><widget class="QLabel" name="assumptions_heading_1"><property name="text"><string>Calculation basis</string></property><property name="styleSheet"><string>font-weight:600; color:#164f8a;</string></property></widget></item><item><widget class="QLabel" name="assumptions_text_1"><property name="textFormat"><enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum></property><property name="text"><string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;&amp;bull; Thin-wall theory applies when R/t &amp;gt; 10, using the mean radius R; otherwise thick-wall Lam&amp;eacute; equations apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;&amp;bull; Thick-wall principal stresses are evaluated together at the bore, where Von Mises and maximum shear stresses are greatest under the adopted model.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;&amp;bull; Under external pressure, radial stress is zero at the bore and compressive at the outer surface. Equivalent stresses are calculated using principal stresses at the same radial location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;&amp;bull; For capped ends, the same geometry, pressure magnitude and uniform axial load give identical Von Mises and maximum shear stresses (where assessed), for internal and external pressure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;&amp;bull; Positive axial load is tension; negative axial load is compression. Temperature derating applies to working pressure only.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string></property><property name="wordWrap"><bool>true</bool></property></widget></item>
<item><spacer name="assumptionsSectionGap2"><property name="orientation"><enum>Qt::Orientation::Vertical</enum></property><property name="sizeType"><enum>QSizePolicy::Fixed</enum></property><property name="sizeHint" stdset="0"><size><width>20</width><height>20</height></size></property></spacer></item><item><widget class="QLabel" name="assumptions_heading_2"><property name="text"><string>Interpretation</string></property><property name="styleSheet"><string>font-weight:600; color:#164f8a;</string></property></widget></item><item><widget class="QLabel" name="assumptions_text_2"><property name="textFormat"><enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum></property><property name="text"><string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;"&gt;• PASS means the individual stress utilisation is no greater than 1.00.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string></property><property name="wordWrap"><bool>true</bool></property></widget></item>
           <item>
            <spacer name="assumptions_inner_spacer">
